    "https://pacific.peopleadmin.com/postings/32843": {
      "title": "University of the Pacific Applicant Portal",
      "description": "University of the Pacific Applicant Portal | Registered Nurse/Clinical Case Manager Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Registered Nurse/Clinical Case Manager Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Registered Nurse/Clinical Case Manager Union Level Department Health Services Campus San Francisco Posting Number 201304383P Full or Part Time Full Time Number of Months 12 Work Schedule Work is generally performed during standard business hours. May be required to work non-business hours. Position End Date Open Date 09/30/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants For Applicants Seeking Job Opportunities within the University Internal: Internal applicants will be considered within the first five (5) business days of the posting period. External: External applicants will be considered on the sixth (6) business day of the posting period. This recruitment will remain open until filled. Sponsorship This position is not eligible for a visa sponsorship now or in the future. Position Summary Information Primary Purpose The Registered Nurse / Clinical Case Manager provides direct clinical nursing care to students while also serving as the coordinating clinician for students with complex, chronic, or high-risk health and behavioral health needs. This dual role blends hands-on nursing practice with longitudinal case management—assessing needs, developing care plans, coordinating services across campus and community resources, and ensuring continuity of care. The position supports the university’s mission of promoting student health, academic success, retention, and wellbeing. Pacific offers full-time employees a unique opportunity to live on our beautiful campus at below-market rental rates—helping you save time and money on your commute. Essential Functions Perform nursing assessments, triage (in person, by phone, and via telehealth), and evaluate acute and chronic health concerns for CAPS and SHS Administer medications, immunizations, injections, perform phlebotomy, and treatments per provider orders and standing orders/protocols. Assist providers with examinations and procedures; perform point-of-care testing, wound care, and specimen collection Provide health education and counseling on topics such as sexual health, mental health, nutrition, substance use, chronic disease self-management, and preventive care. Respond to medical emergencies on campus and initiate appropriate interventions and referrals. Document care accurately and timely in the electronic health record ( EHR ) in compliance with regulatory and professional standards. Support campus public health initiatives, including communicable disease surveillance, outbreak response, and immunization compliance. Attends and contributes to the department staff meetings. Assists staff in preparing outreach/workshop materials. Performs other duties as assigned or requested. Clinical Case Management Identify students with complex medical, mental health, or psychosocial needs. Conduct comprehensive biopsychosocial assessments and develop, implement, and monitor individualized care plans with measurable goals. Coordinate care across wellness departments (counseling and psychological services, services for students with disabilities, dean of students, and external providers (specialists, hospitals, community agencies, insurers). Facilitate care transitions, including hospital discharge follow-up, return-to-campus planning, and referrals to higher levels of care. This position serves as Campus Security Authority ( CSA ) as outlined by the Clery Act. CSAs have federally mandated responsibilities to report crimes that are reported them. University of the Pacific recognizes that diversity, equity, and inclusion is foundational to the success of our valued students and employees. We prioritize policy and decision-making that demonstrates awareness of, and responsiveness to, the ways socio-cultural forces related to race, gender, ability, sexuality, socio-economic status, etc. impede or propel students, faculty and staff. Minimum Qualifications Current, unencumbered Registered Nurse (RN) license in California Bachelor of Science in Nursing ( BSN ) [or Associate degree in Nursing with relevant experience Current BLS certification. Up-to-date titers and Immunizations Minimum of three (3) years of clinical nursing experience; ambulatory, community, public health, inpatient. Minimum of two (2) years of experience in a clinical case management role Demonstrated knowledge of case management principles, care coordination, and community resources. Proficiency with electronic health records and standard office technology. Strong assessment, triage, communication, organizational, and documentation skills. Ability to work independently, manage a caseload, and exercise sound clinical judgment. Preferred Qualifications Five (5) or more years of clinical experience in ambulatory, community, public health, or inpatient settings. Four (4) or more years of experience in a clinical case management role. Case Management certification (e.g., ACM -RN, CMGT -BC) Experience in a college/university health, adolescent/young adult, or behavioral health setting. Knowledge of FERPA and higher-education health service operations. Cultural competence and experience serving diverse student populations Experience and sensitivity in working with people of diverse backgrounds and cultures. Demonstrated experience in advancing social justice, equity, and inclusion in a university setting. Ability to engage and integrate culturally responsive practices and knowledge in their work. Physical Requirements The physical demands described here are representative but not definitive of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this job. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. Frequent sitting and verbal communication with occasional walking and standing. Infrequent bending, stooping, kneeling, or reaching above shoulders. May be expected to lift up to 25 lbs. Use of Personal Protective Equipment ( PPE ) Use of computers, phones, and other technology. Work Environment/Work Week/Travel Work is primarily performed in clinical or office environment, with some outreach performed outdoors or on other campuses. Work is generally performed during standard business hours. May be required to work non-business hours. Moderate travel. Valid driver’s license is required. Incumbent must also be able to meet the University’s fleet rules and be eligible to drive for University business. The University and its insurance carrier reserves the right to exclude applicants based on their driving record. This is an in-person role, and the successful candidate must be willing to relocate within California, preferably within 25 miles of the San Francisco Pacific campus. Hiring Range $52.00 per hour. We consider factors such as, but not limited to, scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s qualifications, internal equity, as well as market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. Background Check Statement All applicants who receive a conditional offer of employment are required to execute a release and authorization for a background screening. AB 810 Misconduct Disclosure Requirement: University of the Pacific complies with California Assembly Bill 810, requiring candidates accepting conditional job offers to disclose any final administrative or judicial findings, ongoing proceedings, allegations, resignations under investigation, or appeals related to sexual harassment or misconduct within the past seven years. Anti-Discrimination/EEO Policy Statement University of the Pacific is an equal opportunity employer dedicated to workforce diversity across backgrounds, experiences, and viewpoints. Pacific does not unlawfully discriminate in its hiring of faculty and staff, or in the provision of its employment benefits to its faculty and staff on the basis of race, color, religion, national origin, ancestry, age, genetic information, sex/gender, marital status, military and veteran status, sexual orientation, medical condition, pregnancy, gender identity, gender expression, or mental or physical disability, or other legally protected characteristics or combination of such characteristics. While we strive to attract a broad and representative pool of candidates, all hiring decisions are made based on merit, selecting the most qualified individual for each position. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a current, unencumbered Registered Nurse (RN) license in California? Yes No * Do you have a Bachelor of Science in Nursing (BSN) [or Associate degree in Nursing with relevant experience]? Yes No * Do you have a current BLS certification? Yes No * Do you have a minimum of three (3) years of clinical nursing experience; ambulatory, community, public health, inpatient? Yes No * Do you have a minimum of two (2) years of experience in a clinical case management role? Yes No * Do you have strong assessment, triage, communication, organizational, and documentation skills? Yes No * Can you work independently, manage a caseload, and exercise sound clinical judgment? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter/Letter of Application Optional Documents Other Document Other Document 2 Other Document 3 University of the Pacific / 3601 Pacific Ave, Stockton, CA 95211 human_resources@pacific.edu human_resources@pacific.edu / 209.946.2124 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://pacific.peopleadmin.com/postings/32851": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Chemistry (Tenure Track)",
      "description": "University of the Pacific Applicant Portal | Assistant Professor of Chemistry (Tenure Track) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Assistant Professor of Chemistry (Tenure Track) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. For Applicants Seeking Job Opportunities within the University Internal: Internal applicants will be considered within the first five (5) business days of the posting period. External: External applicants will be considered on the sixth (6) business day of the posting period. Posting Details Position Information Title Assistant Professor of Chemistry (Tenure Track) Campus Stockton Department Department of Chemistry Posting Number F01108 Full or Part Time Full Time Open Date 09/29/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Days Per Week Weeks Per Year Position Description Primary Purpose and Essential Functions The Department of Chemistry at the University of the Pacific prepares undergraduate and graduate students in the chemical sciences through teaching, year-round undergraduate research, and mentoring of M.S. and Ph.D. students in the Pharmaceutical and Chemical Sciences Program. This tenure-track Assistant Professor of Organic Chemistry supports that mission by teaching core and specialized courses and by building a research program that involves undergraduate and graduate students and is competitive for external funding. Teach Organic Chemistry. Teach General Chemistry. Teach courses in the candidate’s area of specialization at the undergraduate and graduate (M.S. and Ph.D.) levels. Provide academic advising to undergraduate and graduate students. Develop a strong, independent research program suitable for undergraduate and Ph.D. student involvement. Pursue external funding to support the research program. Mentor undergraduate researchers on a year-round basis. Mentor M.S. and Ph.D. students in the Pharmaceutical and Chemical Sciences Program. Participate in departmental and university service as expected of tenure-track faculty. Seek collaborations across the university’s professional schools, including pharmacy, dentistry, and the planned School of Medicine. University of the Pacific recognizes that diversity, equity, and inclusion is foundational to the success of our valued students and employees. We prioritize policy and decision-making that demonstrates awareness of, and responsiveness to, the ways socio-cultural forces related to race, gender, ability, sexuality, socio-economic status, etc. impede or propel students, faculty, and staff. Pacific offers full-time employees a unique opportunity to live on our beautiful campus at below-market rental rates—helping you save time and money on your commute. Minimum Qualifications Ph.D. in chemistry or a closely related field. Preferred Qualifications Postdoctoral training; Research interests in organic chemistry, medicinal chemistry, bioorganic chemistry, or chemical biology. Experience and sensitivity in working with people of diverse backgrounds and cultures. Demonstrated experience in advancing social justice, equity, and inclusion in a university setting. Ability to engage and integrate culturally responsive practices and knowledge in their work. Physical Requirements The physical demands described here are representative but not definitive of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this job. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. This is an in-person role, and the successful candidate must be willing to relocate within California, preferably within 25 miles of the Stockton Pacific campus. Requires extended periods of sitting and repetitive hand/wrist motion while using a computer keyboard and phone. Occasional standing, walking, climbing stairs, bending, stooping, and reaching. Occasional lifting up to 25 pounds. Work Environment/Work Week/Travel: Work is performed during standard hours; Additional hours may be required to meet business needs or deadlines. Hiring Range $78,000 per year. We consider factors such as, but not limited to, scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s qualifications, internal equity, as well as market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. Special Instructions Appointment begins Fall 2027. We encourage interested candidates to apply by October 31, 2026, when we begin reviewing applications. The position will remain open until filled, so we welcome applications throughout the search process. This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Please submit a research proposal suitable for undergraduate and Ph.D. student involvement under Research Program Plan. Contact Information Contact Email Reference Letter Information Are Applicants Required to Submit References for This Posting? Yes Minimum Number of References 3 Maximum Number of References 3 Background Check Statement All applicants who receive a conditional offer of employment are required to execute a release and authorization for a background screening. AB 810 Misconduct Disclosure Requirement: University of the Pacific complies with California Assembly Bill 810, requiring candidates accepting conditional job offers to disclose any final administrative or judicial findings, ongoing proceedings, allegations, resignations under investigation, or appeals related to sexual harassment or misconduct within the past seven years. Anti-Discrimination/EEO Policy Statement University of the Pacific is an equal opportunity employer dedicated to workforce diversity across backgrounds, experiences, and viewpoints. Pacific does not unlawfully discriminate in its hiring of faculty and staff, or in the provision of its employment benefits to its faculty and staff on the basis of race, color, religion, national origin, ancestry, age, genetic information, sex/gender, marital status, military and veteran status, sexual orientation, medical condition, pregnancy, gender identity, gender expression, or mental or physical disability, or other legally protected characteristics or combination of such characteristics. While we strive to attract a broad and representative pool of candidates, all hiring decisions are made based on merit, selecting the most qualified individual for each position. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a Ph.D. in chemistry or a closely related field? Yes No * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? CSHP Job Posting ACCP Job Posting Personal Referral Pacific Website Other Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter/Letter of Application Teaching Philosophy Research Program Plan Optional Documents Other Document Other Document 2 Other Document 3 University of the Pacific / 3601 Pacific Ave, Stockton, CA 95211 human_resources@pacific.edu human_resources@pacific.edu / 209.946.2124 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
