    "https://pacific.peopleadmin.com/postings/32927": {
      "title": "Student Insurance Coordinator",
      "description": "University of the Pacific Applicant Portal | Student Insurance Coordinator Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Student Insurance Coordinator Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Student Insurance Coordinator Union Level Department Health Services Campus Stockton Posting Number 201304391P Full or Part Time Full Time Number of Months 12 Work Schedule Work is primarily performed in a standard office environment. Work performed during standard business hours. Some occasional travel to other campuses may be required. Position End Date Open Date 10/14/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants For Applicants Seeking Job Opportunities within the University Internal: Internal applicants will be considered within the first five (5) business days of the posting period. External: External applicants will be considered on the sixth (6) business day of the posting period. This recruitment will remain open until filled. Sponsorship This position is not eligible for a visa sponsorship now or in the future. Position Summary Information Primary Purpose Under general supervision, the Student Insurance Coordinator is responsible for the implementation and management of the University Student Health Insurance plan across three campuses. Pacific offers full-time employees a unique opportunity to live on our beautiful campus at below-market rental rates—helping you save time and money on your commute. Essential Functions Documents and processes waivers for all students on all campuses verifying eligibility, coverage, deductible, status, etc. and enters findings into appropriate Health Services tracking and medical management programs. Processes and reconciles enrollment for students from all campuses in concert with insurance carrier’s secure site and/or personnel, Health Services medical management programs, and financial management programs. Manually enrolls international students in to all tracking systems. Checks billings for accuracy, submits claims, and generates reports for financial tracking of checks and payments utilizing knowledge of medical coding and Excel spreadsheets. Reconciles payments from insurance carrier. Monitors and maintains the insurance premiums accounting record in conjunction with the appropriate Student Accounts office across all three campuses. Provides back up detail for premium account reconciliation. Assists with electronic on-boarding of new staff members, providing access to Point N Click and acting as liaison with Pacific Technology. Is responsible for updates to Point N Click software when Pac Tech staff is not available. Responsible for updating the Point N Click Dispensary to ensure medication list and prices are accurate for billing. Maintains direct communication with the insurance carrier to resolve claim disputes. Maintains record, prepares forms, verifies information and resolves issues requiring knowledge of the insurance plan. Gives presentations regarding University insurance requirements, Health Services, and the benefits of the student insurance plan on all three campuses. Acts as liaison between student, school, other University departments and insurance company representatives. Monitors Insurance processes to ensure accuracy and adherence to industry, state and federal guidelines. Rebills for denials on claims. Performs other related duties as assigned or requested. University of the Pacific recognizes that diversity, equity, and inclusion is foundational to the success of our valued students and employees. We prioritize policy and decision-making that demonstrates awareness of, and responsiveness to, the ways socio-cultural forces related to race, gender, ability, sexuality, socio-economic status, etc. impede or propel students, faculty, and staff. Minimum Qualifications High School Diploma or GED Two (2) years of work experience in medical billing and coding, accounts receivable, and customer service, or a combination of education and relevant experience. Knowledge of health insurance types ( PPO , HMO , EPO , Medicare), insurance terminologies, insurance verification, and various plan interpretations. Medical Coding and Billing training within 1 (one) year of hire. Proficient in Microsoft Excel or completion of training class within six (6) months of hire. Preferred Qualifications Bachelor’s Degree Certified Revenue Cycle Representative Certification Five (5) or more years of experience in medical billing and coding accounts receivable, and customer service, or a combination of education and relevant experience Experience and sensitivity in working with people of diverse backgrounds and cultures. Demonstrated experience in advancing social justice, equity, and inclusion in a university setting. Ability to engage and integrate culturally responsive practices and knowledge in their work. Physical Requirements The physical demands described here are representative but not definitive of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this job. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. This is an in-person role, and the successful candidate must be willing to relocate within California, preferably within 25 miles of the Stockton Pacific campus. Work performed in typical office environment. Duties require constant sitting and repetitive motion while using computer keyboard and phone. Occasional walking, standing and simple grasping. Occasional climbing stairs, walking across campus, stooping and reaching. Constant communication using both spoken and written means. May be required to lift up to 25 lbs. Work Environment/Work Week/Travel: Work is primarily performed in a standard office environment. Work performed during standard business hours. Some occasional travel to other campuses may be required. Valid driver’s license required. Incumbent must also be able to meet the University’s fleet rules and be eligible to drive for University business. The University and its insurance carrier reserve the right to exclude applicants based on their driving record. Hiring Range $28.00 per hour. We consider factors such as, but not limited to, scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s qualifications, internal equity, as well as market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. Background Check Statement All applicants who receive a conditional offer of employment are required to execute a release and authorization for a background screening. AB 810 Misconduct Disclosure Requirement: University of the Pacific complies with California Assembly Bill 810, requiring candidates accepting conditional job offers to disclose any final administrative or judicial findings, ongoing proceedings, allegations, resignations under investigation, or appeals related to sexual harassment or misconduct within the past seven years. Anti-Discrimination/EEO Policy Statement University of the Pacific is an equal opportunity employer dedicated to workforce diversity across backgrounds, experiences, and viewpoints. Pacific does not unlawfully discriminate in its hiring of faculty and staff, or in the provision of its employment benefits to its faculty and staff on the basis of race, color, religion, national origin, ancestry, age, genetic information, sex/gender, marital status, military and veteran status, sexual orientation, medical condition, pregnancy, gender identity, gender expression, or mental or physical disability, or other legally protected characteristics or combination of such characteristics. While we strive to attract a broad and representative pool of candidates, all hiring decisions are made based on merit, selecting the most qualified individual for each position. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a High School Diploma or GED? Yes No * Do you have two (2) years of work experience in medical billing and coding, accounts receivable, and customer service, or a combination of education and relevant experience? Yes No * Do you have knowledge of health insurance types (PPO, HMO, EPO, Medicare), insurance terminologies, insurance verification, and various plan interpretations? Yes No * Can you complete Medical Coding, Billing training, and Certified Revenue Cycle Representative (CRCR) Certification within 1 year from hire date? Yes No * Are you proficient in Microsoft Excel, or can you complete a training class within six (6) months of hire? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter/Letter of Application Optional Documents Other Document Other Document 2 Other Document 3 University of the Pacific / 3601 Pacific Ave, Stockton, CA 95211 human_resources@pacific.edu human_resources@pacific.edu / 209.946.2124 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
