    "https://pacific.peopleadmin.com/postings/32869": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Mathematics (Tenure Track)",
      "description": "University of the Pacific Applicant Portal | Assistant Professor of Mathematics (Tenure Track) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Assistant Professor of Mathematics (Tenure Track) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. For Applicants Seeking Job Opportunities within the University Internal: Internal applicants will be considered within the first five (5) business days of the posting period. External: External applicants will be considered on the sixth (6) business day of the posting period. Posting Details Position Information Title Assistant Professor of Mathematics (Tenure Track) Campus Stockton Department Department of Mathematics Posting Number F01110 Full or Part Time Full Time Open Date 10/06/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Days Per Week Weeks Per Year Position Description Primary Purpose and Essential Functions The Department of Mathematics at the University of the Pacific invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor position in statistics , beginning Fall 2027. We seek a statistician or applied mathematician who is committed to excellence in undergraduate education and who has demonstrated experience successfully working with diverse student populations. We welcome applicants working in statistics, biostatistics, statistical computing, statistical learning, data science, applied mathematics, or related areas. Priority will be given to candidates whose research interests provide opportunities for interdisciplinary collaboration, particularly with Pacific’s professional schools, such as the Dugoni School of Dentistry, the Long School of Pharmacy, the School of Health Sciences, and the recently announced School of Medicine (to start 2030), as well as with departments in the College of the Pacific, such as Biology. Candidates should be interested in developing collaborative research and grant activities and in involving undergraduate students in research, internships, and other experiential learning opportunities. The position carries a teaching load of five courses per academic year (typically a 3/2 semester load). In addition to teaching, Pacific faculty are expected to maintain an active research program. Faculty in the Department of Mathematics also have opportunities to participate in teaching first-year Core Seminars in the University’s General Education Program. The Department of Mathematics consists of eight full-time tenure-line faculty and five full- or part-time adjunct faculty who provide coursework in mathematics, applied mathematics, and statistics for mathematics and applied mathematics majors, as well as for students across the university. The department offers a collegial and collaborative environment with opportunities for interdisciplinary teaching and research across Pacific’s undergraduate programs and professional schools. The University of the Pacific is a comprehensive, student-centered private university with its main campus located in Stockton, California. The Department of Mathematics is part of the College of the Pacific, which offers programs in the humanities, fine arts, and natural and social sciences. The Stockton campus also includes the Schools of Pharmacy, Engineering & Computer Science, and Business, as well as Benerd College and the Conservatory of Music. Pacific’s Dugoni School of Dentistry is located in San Francisco, while its School of Health Sciences and McGeorge School of Law are located in Sacramento. With a strong emphasis on undergraduate education and close faculty-student collaboration, Pacific provides faculty with opportunities to mentor students through research, internships, and other experiential learning. Pacific offers full-time employees a unique opportunity to live on our beautiful campus at below-market rental rates—helping you save time and money on your commute. Minimum Qualifications Earned Ph.D. in Statistics, Mathematics, Applied Mathematics, or a closely related field is required by August 2027. Experience in teaching undergraduate mathematics, particularly introductory statistics. Preferred Qualifications Experience teaching upper-division statistics courses and electives Experience teaching statistical computing, data science, statistical learning, or related courses Research interests that provide opportunities for interdisciplinary collaboration within the university or with Pacific’s professional schools Experience involving undergraduate students in research or other experiential learning opportunities Physical Requirements The physical demands described here are representative but not definitive of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this job. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. This is an in-person role, and the successful candidate must be willing to relocate within California, preferably within 25 miles of the Stockton Pacific campus. Hiring Range $77,000 per year. We consider factors such as, but not limited to, scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate's qualifications, internal equity, as well as market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. Special Instructions Applicants are required to upload the following documents to their online application: Cover letter stating qualifications and interest in the position. (Please indicate if you are planning to attend the JMM in January 2027 in Chicago.) Curriculum Vitae A teaching statement that includes concrete examples of using real-world data to teach statistics and/or applied mathematics. A statement of research interests. Additionally, applicants are required to provide contact information for two (2) professional references, with at least one (1) reference addressing teaching. Review of applications will begin on November 1, 2026, and continue until the position is filled. Contact Information Christopher Goff, Chair, Department of Mathematics Contact Email cgoff@pacific.edu Reference Letter Information Are Applicants Required to Submit References for This Posting? Yes Minimum Number of References 3 Maximum Number of References 3 Background Check Statement All applicants who receive a conditional offer of employment are required to execute a release and authorization for a background screening. AB 810 Misconduct Disclosure Requirement: University of the Pacific complies with California Assembly Bill 810, requiring candidates accepting conditional job offers to disclose any final administrative or judicial findings, ongoing proceedings, allegations, resignations under investigation, or appeals related to sexual harassment or misconduct within the past seven years. Anti-Discrimination/EEO Policy Statement University of the Pacific is an equal opportunity employer dedicated to workforce diversity across backgrounds, experiences, and viewpoints. Pacific does not unlawfully discriminate in its hiring of faculty and staff, or in the provision of its employment benefits to its faculty and staff on the basis of race, color, religion, national origin, ancestry, age, genetic information, sex/gender, marital status, military and veteran status, sexual orientation, medical condition, pregnancy, gender identity, gender expression, or mental or physical disability, or other legally protected characteristics or combination of such characteristics. While we strive to attract a broad and representative pool of candidates, all hiring decisions are made based on merit, selecting the most qualified individual for each position. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Will you have earned a Ph.D. in Statistics, Mathematics, Applied Mathematics, or a closely related field by August 2027? Yes No * Do you have experience in teaching undergraduate mathematics, particularly introductory statistics? Yes No * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? CSHP Job Posting ACCP Job Posting Personal Referral Pacific Website Other Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter/Letter of Application Teaching Philosophy Research Program Plan Optional Documents Other Document Other Document 2 University of the Pacific / 3601 Pacific Ave, Stockton, CA 95211 human_resources@pacific.edu human_resources@pacific.edu / 209.946.2124 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://pacific.peopleadmin.com/postings/32933": {
      "title": "Central Sterilization Processing &amp; Dispensary Operations Manager",
      "description": "University of the Pacific Applicant Portal | Central Sterilization Processing &amp; Dispensary Operations Manager Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Central Sterilization Processing & Dispensary Operations Manager Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Central Sterilization Processing & Dispensary Operations Manager Union Level Department Dental Clinic Central Sterilization Campus San Francisco Posting Number 201304392P Full or Part Time Full Time Number of Months 12 Work Schedule M-F (8) hours per day Position End Date Open Date 10/15/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants For Applicants Seeking Job Opportunities within the University Internal: Internal applicants will be considered within the first five (5) business days of the posting period. External: External applicants will be considered on the sixth (6) business day of the posting period. For in-person roles: This is an in-person role, and the successful candidate must be willing to relocate within California, preferably within 25 miles of the (City) Pacific campus. For online roles: While this is an online position, Pacific’s three campuses are within California and its faculty and staff are mostly California residents. For administrative purposes, California residents are preferred. Out of state hires must be approved either by the Provost and Executive Vice President for Academic Affairs (for academic hires) or by the Chief Financial Officer and Executive Vice President for Finance and Operations. Sponsorship This position is not eligible for a visa sponsorship now or in the future. Position Summary Information Primary Purpose Under the general supervision of the Director of Clinic Operations, provides leadership and management of Central Sterilization Processing and Dispensing Operations, including personnel, inventory, equipment, infection prevention practices, and operational workflows. Ensures compliance with regulatory and accreditation standards, supports clinical education and patient care activities, and promotes operational excellence through quality improvement, staff development, and effective resource management. University of the Pacific recognizes that diversity, equity, and inclusion is foundational to the success of our valued students and employees. We prioritize policy and decision-making that demonstrates awareness of, and responsiveness to, the ways socio-cultural forces related to race, gender, ability, sexuality, socio-economic status, etc. impede or propel students, faculty, and staff. Essential Functions Manage sterilization/dispensing staff to include hiring, training, staff development, work distribution, performance evaluations, scheduling, coaching, recognition, and corrective action. Coordinate staffing coverage for all sterilization, dispensing, and inventory management areas and collaborate with clinical managers to ensure efficient clinic operations. Demonstrate exceptional customer service and establish service standards for staff. Participate in Infection Control, Clinic Operations, and other assigned committees. Plan, direct, monitor, troubleshoot, and evaluate sterilization, dispensing, inventory, and instrument tracking operations. Ensure compliance with infection prevention requirements, regulatory standards, clinic policies, and accreditation expectations. Supervise decontamination, high-level disinfection, packaging, sterilization, storage, distribution, and inventory control activities. Develop and monitor quality assurance, competency validation, infection prevention, and operational improvement programs. Ensure adequate staffing, competency assessment, ongoing education, and professional development programs are maintained. Oversee equipment maintenance, preventive maintenance schedules, repairs, biological monitoring, and sterilization documentation. Maintain accurate inventories of instruments, supplies, materials, and equipment and ensure inventory security and accountability. Administer electronic instrument tracking systems and utilize operational data for reporting and process improvement. Support student clinical education through training, operational support, and compliance oversight. Provide leadership in accomplishing strategic and operational objectives of the School of Dentistry. Perform other duties as assigned by the Director of Clinic Operations. Minimum Qualifications Knowledge of: Sterilization techniques and instrument reprocessing workflows. Infection control protocols, standards, and regulatory requirements. Advanced knowledge of dental instruments, equipment, terminology, procedures, and materials. Electronic instrument tracking systems, inventory systems, and barcode technology. Intermediate knowledge of Microsoft 365 applications including Outlook, Word, Excel, PowerPoint, Teams, and SharePoint. Ability to: Produce professional reports and correspondence. Utilize Microsoft 365 applications for reporting, presentations, communication, and data analysis. Interpret operational metrics and implement process improvements. Lead large teams across multiple service areas. Communicate effectively with faculty, staff, students, patients, vendors, and leadership. Experience: Minimum five (5) years of progressive management experience in a dental, medical, hospital, or healthcare setting leading large teams and overseeing multiple clinical, sterilization, dispensing, or operational areas. Demonstrated experience with workforce planning, employee development, scheduling, coaching, engagement, and performance management. Previous experience working in central sterilization serving a large-scale healthcare, hospital, academic dental, or healthcare delivery system environment. Experience collaborating with clinical leadership and cross-functional stakeholders. Education/Certification: High school diploma or equivalent required. Current sterilization certification/license required from HSPA or CBSPD Possession of a Registered Dental Assistant ( RDA ) license does not substitute for the sterilization certification requirement. Certification in Central Sterilization Management required or must be obtained within twelve (12) months of employment. Working Conditions: Position is full-time, 5 days per week, 8 hours per day. Occasional overtime required. Occupational exposure to blood borne pathogens may reasonably be anticipated.  Personal protective equipment will be provided to reduce or eliminate exposure to infectious agents. Preferred Qualifications Knowledge of: Dental management systems, instrument tracking technologies, and inventory management systems. Advanced understanding of infection prevention, regulatory compliance, and quality assurance principles. Experince managing Union team. Ability to: Provide leadership and direction to staff and student employees. Lead quality improvement and operational excellence initiatives. Experience: Experience supporting student clinical education. Experience managing centralized sterilization and distribution services. Experience with large-scale instrument inventory systems. Familiarity with dental management systems and tracking technologies. Experience developing training programs for students and staff. Experience leading regulatory compliance, infection prevention, and process improvement initiatives. Education/Certification: Bachelor’s degree in healthcare administration, Public Health, Healthcare Management, or a related field preferred. Registered Dental Assistant ( RDA ) license preferred. Certification in Infection Prevention and Control ( CIC ), Certified Healthcare Leader ( CHL ), or related certification preferred. Other: Experience and sensitivity in working with people of diverse backgrounds and cultures. Demonstrated experience in advancing social justice, equity, and inclusion in a university setting. Ability to engage and integrate culturally responsive practices and knowledge in their work. Physical Requirements The physical demands described here are representative but not definitive of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this job. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. Requires standing during the majority of working hours. Requires lifting instrument baskets, supplies, and materials up to 40 pounds. Requires movement of carts and equipment throughout clinic facilities. Occupational exposure to bloodborne pathogens may reasonably be anticipated; appropriate personal protective equipment will be provided. Hiring Range $85,500.00 - $101,500.00 per year. We consider factors such as, but not limited to, scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s qualifications, internal equity, as well as market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. Background Check Statement All applicants who receive a conditional offer of employment are required to execute a release and authorization for a background screening. AB 810 Misconduct Disclosure Requirement: University of the Pacific complies with California Assembly Bill 810, requiring candidates accepting conditional job offers to disclose any final administrative or judicial findings, ongoing proceedings, allegations, resignations under investigation, or appeals related to sexual harassment or misconduct within the past seven years. Anti-Discrimination/EEO Policy Statement University of the Pacific is an equal opportunity employer dedicated to workforce diversity across backgrounds, experiences, and viewpoints. Pacific does not unlawfully discriminate in its hiring of faculty and staff, or in the provision of its employment benefits to its faculty and staff on the basis of race, color, religion, national origin, ancestry, age, genetic information, sex/gender, marital status, military and veteran status, sexual orientation, medical condition, pregnancy, gender identity, gender expression, or mental or physical disability, or other legally protected characteristics or combination of such characteristics. While we strive to attract a broad and representative pool of candidates, all hiring decisions are made based on merit, selecting the most qualified individual for each position. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently authorized to work in the U.S. without the need for sponsorship now or in the future (for ex but not limited to H1B, TN, J1)? Yes No * How did you first learn about this employment opportunity? University of the Pacific Website Asianlife.com Blackperspective.com CentralValleyJobs.com Craigslist Dice.com Higheredjobs.com Hispanic-Jobs.com Indeed.com Insidehighered.com LinkedIn Lgbtconnect.com Metrochamber.org Monster.com Thelaa.org SimplyHired.com Workplacediversity.com Association of American Colleges and Universities (AAC&U) Chronicle of HIgher Education Diverse Issues in Higher Education EDUCAUSE Higher Education Recruitment Consortium (HERC) Higher Education Recruitment Consortium - Northern California (NorCal HERC) Modesto Bee Pacific Employee Personal Referral Professional or Association Listserv Publication or website from a professional organization Sacramento Bee San Francisco Chronicle Stockton Record Agency Referral Other Online Job Board * Pacific participates in federal healthcare programs. As such, a required part of the hiring process is to verify that potential employees have not been excluded from participating in federal programs for mandatory exclusions (including for fraud, controlled substances crimes, patient abuse or neglect, or other program-related crimes) or for other permissive exclusions by the Office of Inspector General. A \"Yes\" response would be considered disqualifying. Please answer the following question accordingly: \n\nAre you currently excluded from participation in federal programs (including Medicare, Medicaid, or any other federal healthcare program)? Yes No * Pacific participates in federal healthcare programs. As such, a required part of the hiring process is to verify that potential employees have not been excluded from participating in federal programs for mandatory exclusions (including for fraud, controlled substances crimes, patient abuse or neglect, or other program-related crimes) or for other permissive exclusions by the Office of Inspector General. A \"Yes\" response would be considered disqualifying. Please answer the following question accordingly: \n\nHave you received notice that you are under review for possible exclusion from any federal programs (including Medicare, Medicaid, or any other federal healthcare program)? Yes No * Do you have a minimum five (5) years of progressive management experience in a dental, medical, hospital, or healthcare setting leading large teams and overseeing\nmultiple clinical, sterilization, dispensing, or operational areas? (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter/Letter of Application Dental Certifications Optional Documents Other Document University of the Pacific / 3601 Pacific Ave, Stockton, CA 95211 human_resources@pacific.edu human_resources@pacific.edu / 209.946.2124 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
