    "https://pacific.peopleadmin.com/postings/32969": {
      "title": "Administrative Assistant II",
      "description": "University of the Pacific Applicant Portal | Administrative Assistant II Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Administrative Assistant II Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Administrative Assistant II Union Level Department Benerd College Campus Stockton Posting Number 201304396P Full or Part Time Full Time Number of Months 12 Work Schedule Work is performed during standard hours; additional hours may be required to meet business needs or deadlines. Position End Date Open Date 10/26/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants For Applicants Seeking Job Opportunities within the University Internal: Internal applicants will be considered within the first five (5) business days of the posting period. External: External applicants will be considered on the sixth (6) business day of the posting period. This recruitment will remain open until filled. Sponsorship This position is not eligible for a visa sponsorship now or in the future. Position Summary Information Primary Purpose The Administrative Assistant II provides administrative and operational support to the Dean’s Office and Benerd College. The position assists with day-to-day office functions, personnel and student employment processes, financial transactions, records and document preparation, purchasing, scheduling, events, and other administrative activities. The position works collaboratively with faculty, staff, students, and university departments to support efficient and effective college operations. Essential Functions Provides general administrative support to the Dean’s Office, faculty, and staff, including preparing correspondence, maintaining records and files, coordinating documents, and responding to routine inquiries. Assists with faculty and student employment processes, including updating position descriptions, preparing appointment letters and job postings, collecting required documentation, and supporting completion of hiring transactions. Assists with reviewing and processing timesheets and other payroll-related documentation for part-time faculty and student employees. Prepares and processes routine payroll vouchers and other administrative forms. Assists with routine financial transactions, including invoice processing, purchase requisitions, purchase orders, reimbursements, and other purchasing activities. Assists with reviewing and processing transactions in Chrome River and other university financial systems. Supports routine reconciliation activities by organizing documentation, reviewing transactions, and identifying discrepancies for appropriate follow-up. Assists with daily cashiering activities and other routine financial administrative processes in coordination with appropriate university staff. Maintains records and documentation related to agreements, contracts, memoranda of understanding, and other departmental administrative records. Coordinates office supplies, purchasing requests, equipment needs, and routine building or facilities requests. Assists faculty and appropriate university offices with administrative processes related to student scholarships, including maintaining records and tracking required information. Provides administrative support for accreditation and assessment activities, including organizing records, collecting documentation, maintaining files, scheduling activities, and assisting with preparation of materials. Assists with planning and coordinating meetings, events, and other college activities, including scheduling, communications, logistics, materials, and related administrative support. Uses university systems and Microsoft Office applications to enter, maintain, retrieve, and prepare information and reports. Performs other related duties as assigned. University of the Pacific recognizes that diversity, equity, and inclusion is foundational to the success of our valued students and employees. We prioritize policy and decision-making that demonstrates awareness of, and responsiveness to, the ways socio-cultural forces related to race, gender, ability, sexuality, socio-economic status, etc. impede or propel students, faculty, and staff. Pacific offers full-time employees a unique opportunity to live on our beautiful campus at below-market rental rates—helping you save time and money on your commute. Minimum Qualifications Minimum Qualifications Equivalent combination of relevant work experience and education where two (2) years of full-time experience in the same/similar position is equal to one (1) year of completed post high school coursework. Two (2) years of post-high school education. Two (2) years of responsible administrative experience. Preferred Qualifications Bachelor’s Degree. Experience providing administrative support in an office or professional environment. Experience using Microsoft Word, Excel, Outlook, and other office productivity applications. Strong organizational skills and excellent attention to detail. Effective written and verbal communication skills. Demonstrated customer service skills and ability to interact professionally with a variety of individuals. Ability to organize and prioritize multiple assignments and meet established deadlines. Ability to maintain accurate records and handle sensitive or confidential information appropriately. Ability to learn and use administrative, financial, and records-management systems. Experience processing purchasing, payroll, personnel, or other administrative transactions. Experience working in a higher education environment. Ability to coordinate a variety of activities, correctly interpret directions, and work well under tight deadlines is crucial. Experience with university administrative systems such as Banner, Chrome River, OnBase, Salesforce, or similar systems. Experience and sensitivity in working with people of diverse backgrounds and cultures. Demonstrated experience in advancing social justice, equity, and inclusion in a university setting. Ability to engage and integrate culturally responsive practices and knowledge in their work. Physical Requirements The physical demands described here are representative but not definitive of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this job. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. Requires extended periods of sitting and repetitive hand/wrist motion while using a computer keyboard and phone. Occasional standing, walking, climbing stairs, bending, stooping, and reaching. Occasional lifting up to 25 pounds. Work is performed during standard hours; additional hours may be required to meet business needs or deadlines. Hiring Range $18.99 - 23.74 per hour. We consider factors such as, but not limited to, scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s qualifications, internal equity, as well as market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. Background Check Statement All applicants who receive a conditional offer of employment are required to execute a release and authorization for a background screening. AB 810 Misconduct Disclosure Requirement: University of the Pacific complies with California Assembly Bill 810, requiring candidates accepting conditional job offers to disclose any final administrative or judicial findings, ongoing proceedings, allegations, resignations under investigation, or appeals related to sexual harassment or misconduct within the past seven years. Anti-Discrimination/EEO Policy Statement University of the Pacific is an equal opportunity employer dedicated to workforce diversity across backgrounds, experiences, and viewpoints. Pacific does not unlawfully discriminate in its hiring of faculty and staff, or in the provision of its employment benefits to its faculty and staff on the basis of race, color, religion, national origin, ancestry, age, genetic information, sex/gender, marital status, military and veteran status, sexual orientation, medical condition, pregnancy, gender identity, gender expression, or mental or physical disability, or other legally protected characteristics or combination of such characteristics. While we strive to attract a broad and representative pool of candidates, all hiring decisions are made based on merit, selecting the most qualified individual for each position. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have an equivalent combination of relevant work experience and education where two (2) years of full-time experience in the same/similar position is equal to one (1) year of completed post high school coursework? Yes No * Do you have two (2) years of post-high school education? Yes No * Do you have two (2) years of responsible administrative experience? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter/Letter of Application Optional Documents Other Document Other Document 2 Other Document 3 University of the Pacific / 3601 Pacific Ave, Stockton, CA 95211 human_resources@pacific.edu human_resources@pacific.edu / 209.946.2124 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://pacific.peopleadmin.com/postings/32941": {
      "title": "Sterilization/Dispensing Technician",
      "description": "University of the Pacific Applicant Portal | Sterilization/Dispensing Technician Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Sterilization/Dispensing Technician Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Sterilization/Dispensing Technician Union Level Department PHCC Sacramento Clinic Campus Sacramento Posting Number 201304394P Full or Part Time Full Time Number of Months 12 Work Schedule Position is full-time, 8 hours hours per day, five (5) days per week. Must be available to work varying shifts to include evenings. Position End Date Open Date Close Date Open Until Filled No Special Instructions to Applicants For Applicants Seeking Job Opportunities within the University Internal: Internal applicants will be considered within the first five (5) business days of the posting period. External: External applicants will be considered on the sixth (6) business day of the posting period. Sponsorship This position is not eligible for a visa sponsorship now or in the future. Position Summary Information Primary Purpose Under the immediate supervision of the Clinic Manager, performs duties related to infection control and the sterilization and dispensing areas. University of the Pacific recognizes that diversity, equity, and inclusion is foundational to the success of our valued students and employees. We prioritize policy and decision-making that demonstrates awareness of, and responsiveness to, the ways socio-cultural forces related to race, gender, ability, sexuality, socio-economic status, etc. impede or propel students, faculty, and staff. Essential Functions Process dental instruments and equipment to include receiving, cleaning, wrapping, and sterilization of semi-critical and critical items; disinfect non-critical portable dental equipment; inspect contents of all instrument cassettes and packages for completeness and damage; replace as needed. Operate and assist in the maintenance of washing and cleaning sterilization machines including weekly biological testing of autoclaves. Prepare pre-packaged disposable items; dispense instrument cassettes and dental materials/equipment according to established procedures. Maintain an accurate inventory of borrowed and returned cassettes, materials, and equipment; maintain security of all inventories according to established procedures. Order supplies for dispensing windows; restock inventory as needed. Maintain a neat, clean, and orderly sterilization room and dispensing area according to established standards. Perform other duties as assigned by the PHCC Assistant Dental Director and the Director. Minimum Qualifications Minimum of one year of experience in a dental/medical setting. High school diploma or equivalent. Certification in Central Sterilization required or obtain within 12 months of employment Preferred Qualifications Experience: Previous experience in a hospital or health care delivery system is highly desirable. Knowledge of: Sterilization techniques. Dental instruments/materials and their use. Dental terminology and procedures. Infection control protocol and requirements. Ability to: Index and alphabetize accurately. Recognize and set-up dental instruments. Use electronic tracking system using bar coding, scanners, and reports provided by tracking software. Communicate effectively with faculty, staff and patients. Effectively provide assistance to staff and faculty. Maintain a professional demeanor at all times. Apply time management skills. Demonstrate initiative and sound judgment in fast paced environment. Work independently or as part of a team. Other: Experience and sensitivity in working with people of diverse backgrounds and cultures. Demonstrated experience in advancing social justice, equity, and inclusion in a university setting. Ability to engage and integrate culturally responsive practices and knowledge in their work. Physical Requirements The physical demands described here are representative but not definitive of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this job. Requires standing during most working hours. Requires lifting of instrument baskets in and out of autoclave machine and lifting boxes of gloves and dental materials up to 40 lbs. Requires moving large mobile carts through clinic areas. Hiring Range $20.16 - $26.70 per hour We consider factors such as, but not limited to, scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s qualifications, internal equity, as well as market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. Background Check Statement All applicants who receive a conditional offer of employment are required to execute a release and authorization for a background screening. AB 810 Misconduct Disclosure Requirement: University of the Pacific complies with California Assembly Bill 810, requiring candidates accepting conditional job offers to disclose any final administrative or judicial findings, ongoing proceedings, allegations, resignations under investigation, or appeals related to sexual harassment or misconduct within the past seven years. Anti-Discrimination/EEO Policy Statement University of the Pacific is an equal opportunity employer dedicated to workforce diversity across backgrounds, experiences, and viewpoints. Pacific does not unlawfully discriminate in its hiring of faculty and staff, or in the provision of its employment benefits to its faculty and staff on the basis of race, color, religion, national origin, ancestry, age, genetic information, sex/gender, marital status, military and veteran status, sexual orientation, medical condition, pregnancy, gender identity, gender expression, or mental or physical disability, or other legally protected characteristics or combination of such characteristics. While we strive to attract a broad and representative pool of candidates, all hiring decisions are made based on merit, selecting the most qualified individual for each position. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a high school diploma or GED? Yes No * Do you have at least a minimum of one (1) year of experience in a dental/medical setting? Yes No * Do you have a certification in Central Sterilization or are you willing to obtain one within twelve (12) months of employment? Yes No * Pacific participates in federal healthcare programs. As such, a required part of the hiring process is to verify that potential employees have not been excluded from participating in federal programs for mandatory exclusions (including for fraud, controlled substances crimes, patient abuse or neglect, or other program-related crimes) or for other permissive exclusions by the Office of Inspector General. A \"Yes\" response would be considered disqualifying. Please answer the following question accordingly: \r\n\r\nAre you currently excluded from participation in federal programs (including Medicare, Medicaid, or any other federal healthcare program)? Yes No * Pacific participates in federal healthcare programs. As such, a required part of the hiring process is to verify that potential employees have not been excluded from participating in federal programs for mandatory exclusions (including for fraud, controlled substances crimes, patient abuse or neglect, or other program-related crimes) or for other permissive exclusions by the Office of Inspector General. A \"Yes\" response would be considered disqualifying. Please answer the following question accordingly: \r\n\r\nHave you received notice that you are under review for possible exclusion from any federal programs (including Medicare, Medicaid, or any other federal healthcare program)? Yes No * Pacific participates in federal healthcare programs. As such, a required part of the hiring process is to verify that potential employees have not been excluded from participating in federal programs for mandatory exclusions (including for fraud, controlled substances crimes, patient abuse or neglect, or other program-related crimes) or for other permissive exclusions by the Office of Inspector General. A \"Yes\" response would be considered disqualifying. Please answer the following question accordingly: Are you currently excluded from participation in federal programs (including Medicare, Medicaid, or any other federal healthcare program)? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter/Letter of Application Optional Documents Other Document University of the Pacific / 3601 Pacific Ave, Stockton, CA 95211 human_resources@pacific.edu human_resources@pacific.edu / 209.946.2124 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
